use to re-deploy modal_app: python -m modal deploy backend/modal_app.py
backend is all in modal, but included in this package for future revisions.
model endpoint is https://adrian-jackson--cranberry-inspector-cranberryinspector-predict.modal.run

One-time setup (before first deploy after the API-key change):
  modal secret create cranberry-api-key API_KEY=<paste a generated key>
  # generate one with: python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"
Share that same key value with whoever you want to have access — they paste it
into the "access key" prompt the frontend shows on first visit (it's stored in
their browser's localStorage, not baked into the Vercel build).

If SAM3 needs to be updated later, bump SAM3_COMMIT in backend/modal_app.py to
the new commit SHA from https://github.com/facebookresearch/sam3 and redeploy.